@lang en
IMPORT `bm-ear-part2-third-party`

-- Traces of the regulative rules (bm-ear-duties.l4). A trace's result is printed, not
-- asserted (a DEONTIC cannot be compared); the expected result is written above each
-- trace, from the text, and NOTES.md section 6 records what the run printed. The clock is
-- in calendar days: day 0 is the occurrence (General Condition 5) or the day the written
-- request was sent (General Condition 7).

§ `Tests: the regulative rules`

§§ `General Condition 5: notice, inspection, repair`

-- Notice received on day 14; damage not minor; reasonable time 10 days; Bao Minh inspects
-- on day 20; the Insured repairs on day 25. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `General Condition 5: notice, then inspection, then repair` FALSE 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `give notice of the occurrence` AT 14
    PARTY `Bao Minh` DOES `inspect the loss` AT 20
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `repair or replace the damaged item` AT 25

-- No notice by day 15. Expected: BREACH BY the Insured, "General Condition 5: Bao Minh
-- received no notice within 14 days of the occurrence, and is not liable for the loss".
#TRACE `General Condition 5: notice, then inspection, then repair` FALSE 10 AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 15)

-- Notice on day 3; Bao Minh does not inspect within the reasonable time (10 days from
-- notice, so by day 13); the Insured repairs on day 30. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `General Condition 5: notice, then inspection, then repair` FALSE 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `give notice of the occurrence` AT 3
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 14)
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `repair or replace the damaged item` AT 30

-- Minor damage: after notice on day 2 the Insured may repair at once. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `General Condition 5: notice, then inspection, then repair` TRUE 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `give notice of the occurrence` AT 2
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `repair or replace the damaged item` AT 2

-- (e) The police duty has no deadline: nothing done by day 400 leaves it standing.
-- Expected: the residual obligation printed back.
#TRACE `General Condition 5(e): inform the police of a theft` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `General Condition 4(b): material change`

-- A change made WITH written approval is not the forbidden act; the prohibition stands.
-- Expected: the residual prohibition.
#TRACE `General Condition 4(b): no material change increasing the risk without written approval` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `make or admit a material change that increases the risk` TRUE AT 30

-- A change made WITHOUT approval, on day 200. Expected: BREACH BY the Insured.
#TRACE `General Condition 4(b): no material change increasing the risk without written approval` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `make or admit a material change that increases the risk` FALSE AT 200

#TRACE `General Condition 4(b): notify a material change` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `notify Bao Minh of a material change, by telegram and in writing` AT 1

§§ `General Condition 7: appointing an arbitrator`

-- A request sent on 31 January 2026 allows 28 days (to 28 February); on 15 March 2026,
-- 31 days (to 15 April).
#ASSERT `General Condition 7: the days allowed to appoint after a request sent on` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `General Condition 7: the days allowed to appoint after a request sent on` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS 31

-- Bao Minh, asked on 31 January 2026, appoints on day 28. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `General Condition 7: the party asked,` `Bao Minh` `, must appoint an arbitrator after a request sent on` (YMD 2026 1 31) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Bao Minh` DOES `appoint an arbitrator in writing` AT 28

-- Bao Minh never appoints. Expected: BREACH BY Bao Minh, with the reason that the policy
-- states no consequence (Finding 7).
#TRACE `General Condition 7: the party asked,` `Bao Minh` `, must appoint an arbitrator after a request sent on` (YMD 2026 1 31) AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 29)

§§ `Part II conditions 1 and 2`

-- An admission with Bao Minh's written consent: not the forbidden act. Expected: residual.
#TRACE `Part II condition 1: no admission without written consent` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `make an admission, offer, promise, payment or indemnity` TRUE AT 5

-- An admission without consent. Expected: BREACH BY the Insured.
#TRACE `Part II condition 1: no admission without written consent` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `make an admission, offer, promise, payment or indemnity` FALSE AT 5

-- Bao Minh's power to take over the defence, exercised. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `Part II condition 1: Bao Minh may take over the defence or settlement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Bao Minh` DOES `take over the defence or settlement of the claim` AT 3

-- Bao Minh pays the limit under condition 2. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `Part II condition 2: Bao Minh may pay the limit or a settlement sum` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Bao Minh` DOES `pay the limit of indemnity less sums already paid, or a lesser sum for which the claims can be settled` AT 40
